menu "Links: one hub, many radios (ATTACHMENT-DESIGN)"

config MESHTASTIC_LINK_CODEC
	bool
	default y if MESHTASTIC_HUB || MESHTASTIC_WORKER || MESHTASTIC_WORKER_RX
	help
	  The envelope a worker and its hub exchange (pure byte packing).
	  Pulled in by anything that speaks it; not a user choice.

config MESHTASTIC_LINK_BEARER
	bool
	default y if MESHTASTIC_LINK_CODEC
	help
	  The board-to-board link between a hub and its workers (ATTACHMENT-SCOPE §4):
	  a registry of bearers -- the BLE peer link, a wire, a test pipe -- each
	  a send and a link_info. Envelopes never see a bearer's types.

config MESHTASTIC_HUB
	bool "This node is a hub: it hears through workers"
	default n
	help
	  Accept link envelopes over the BLE peer link. A worker's RX_FRAME
	  enters the router as an RF frame tagged with the worker's preset and
	  signal; the node's identity, keys, NodeDB and modules stay exactly as
	  they are. Costs a small table (MESHTASTIC_HUB_WORKERS_MAX entries) and
	  8 B per RX queue slot; the code is flash.

config MESHTASTIC_HUB_WORKERS_MAX
	int "Workers a hub tracks (its own radio is not counted)"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_HUB
	default 4
	range 1 8
	help
	  A BLE peer link per worker; the R8 has 3 connection slots in total.

config MESHTASTIC_HUB_EVICT_SEC
	int "Seconds a worker stays in the table after its link went down"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_HUB
	default 180
	range 1 3600
	help
	  A worker whose bearer link dropped keeps its slot (and counters) this long
	  so a reboot or a BLE hiccup re-admits it in place; after that the slot
	  is freed. A worker that speaks again before then is simply up again.

config MESHTASTIC_HUB_ALLOW_MAX
	int "Operator allow-list entries (workers admitted on an untrusted link)"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_HUB
	default 4
	range 1 8

config MESHTASTIC_WORKER
	bool "This node is a keyless worker"
	depends on !MESHTASTIC_HUB
	default n
	help
	  The radio forwards every frame it hears, undecoded, with its RSSI/SNR
	  and preset, to its hub over the peer link (overlay-ble-peer.conf; on
	  native_sim the send is a test seam), and retunes when the hub says
	  so. Transmit for the hub is phase 3. The image carries no channel
	  keys, no PKI, no NodeDB and no config beyond its preset and its hub:
	  build with samples/meshtastic/overlay-worker.conf, whose
	  post-build step refuses an image in which any of those linked
	  (cmake/keyless-assert.cmake). The router is never reached from the
	  radio on a worker; origination is refused at the outbound queue.

config MESHTASTIC_WORKER_HUB_ID
	hex "The hub's node number (0 = set at runtime)"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_WORKER
	default 0
	help
	  Baked-in hub. `meshtastic worker hub <id>` overrides it and the
	  value persists (mtattach/brain) with MESHTASTIC_SETTINGS.

config MESHTASTIC_WORKER_STATUS_PERIOD_SEC
	int "STATUS report period (s)"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_WORKER
	default 60
	range 5 3600

config MESHTASTIC_WORKER_TX_STACK_SIZE
	int "Stack of the worker's transmit thread (bytes)"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_WORKER
	default 2048
	help
	  A transmit blocks for the frame's airtime (and its contention wait),
	  so it runs on its own thread: the forward path -- the RX thread's
	  queue and the work item that writes envelopes to the hub -- must
	  keep draining while the radio is keyed up, or a busy preset overflows
	  the worker's RX queue. Sized like the hub's outbound worker.

config MESHTASTIC_WORKER_TX_QUEUE_SIZE
	int "Frames the hub has handed this worker, waiting to key up"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_WORKER
	default 4
	range 1 16
	help
	  TX_FRAMEs accepted from the hub and not yet transmitted. A full queue
	  refuses the envelope (counted; the hub sees no TX_RESULT). Each entry
	  is a full airframe.

config MESHTASTIC_WORKER_QUEUE_SIZE
	int "Frames queued for the hub"
	depends on MESHTASTIC_WORKER
	default 4
	range 1 16
	help
	  Between the RX thread and the forwarding work item. ~260 B each.

endmenu
